# DIT-OS NASM assembly

Before editing matching files, read `.agents/skills/nasm-assembly/SKILL.md` and follow
it. Also apply `AGENTS.md` (definition of done, handoff, hard rules) and the
mandatory `.agents/skills/security-audit/SKILL.md` for every code change.
Content lives in the skill; this file only points to it.

Never forget:
- Every file declares bits 16 or bits 32; never elf64.
- Save every register on interrupt entry; preserve EBX, ESI, EDI, EBP.
- Keep context.asm frame layout in sync with fork/task creation.
- Name constants; shared boot constants live in bootloader/src/common/constants.inc.
